fix(mcp): support WebMCP source-based tool ownership (#25507)

## Background

Chrome 160 exposes WebMCP tool owners as `source` instead of `window`,
causing same-named tools in different frames to share aliases and route
calls to the wrong frame. Fixes #25460; reported and diagnosed by
@jagreehal.

## Summary

Use `tool.source ?? tool.window` for alias lookup and storage, and make
both owner fields optional. Add a regression test for unique aliases,
stable aliases after rediscovery, and correct frame routing; add one
patch changeset.

The new test failed before the fix; all 22 transport tests pass
afterward with `pnpm --filter @ai-sdk/mcp test:node
src/tool/webmcp-transport.test.ts`. `pnpm type-check
--filter=@ai-sdk/mcp`, lint, formatting, and diff checks pass.

## End-to-End Verification

Chrome 160 browser verification could not run because Canary 160 is
unavailable here. The local public-API reproduction below uses simulated
browser descriptors and this checkout's freshly bundled MCP source;
provider-utils uses its existing local workspace build. This is not live
browser verification.

Before: `getCart`, `getCart`; both calls reach the iframe;
`createMCPTools` throws a duplicate-name error. After: `getCart`,
`getCart_2`; each reaches its own frame; `createMCPTools` succeeds.

<details>
<summary>Complete local reproduction and execution commands</summary>

Requires this checkout's installed esbuild 0.28.1 and local workspace
dependencies. The following bundle and execution commands were run
before and after the fix, from the repository root:

```sh
node --input-type=module -e 'import { build } from "./node_modules/.pnpm/esbuild@0.28.1/node_modules/esbuild/lib/main.js"; await build({entryPoints:["packages/mcp/src/index.ts"], bundle:true, platform:"node", format:"esm", packages:"external", define:{__PACKAGE_VERSION__:JSON.stringify("2.0.104")}, outfile:"packages/mcp/dist/issue-25460.mjs"});'
node /tmp/ai-25460/repro.mjs
```

Save this script as `/tmp/ai-25460/repro.mjs` (adjust the checkout path
when necessary):

```js
import {
  createMCPClient,
  createMCPTools,
  Experimental_WebMCPTransport as WebMCPTransport,
} from '/Users/aayushkapoor/Desktop/ai/packages/mcp/dist/issue-25460.mjs';

const tools = ['page', 'iframe'].map(frame => ({
  name: 'getCart',
  description: frame,
  origin: 'https://shop.example',
  source: {},
}));
const client = await createMCPClient({
  transport: new WebMCPTransport({
    modelContext: {
      getTools: async () => tools,
      executeTool: async tool => JSON.stringify({ from: tool.description }),
    },
  }),
});
try {
  const { tools: definitions } = await client.listTools();
  console.log('names:', definitions.map(tool => tool.name));
  for (const { name } of definitions) {
    console.log(name, (await client.callTool({ name })).content);
  }
  console.log('createMCPTools:', Object.keys(createMCPTools(definitions)));
} finally {
  await client.close();
}
```

</details>

